[627.690771, "o", "============================================================\r\n Adaptive Rejection Sampler (Gilks & Wild 1992) test suite\r\n============================================================\r\n\r\n[1] Sampling 5000 draws from N(0,1) via ars(dnorm, c(-Inf, Inf)) ...\r\n    expected mean = 0, sd = 1; Kolmogorov-Smirnov p-value = 0.7173\r\nNORMAL_TEST: PASS (mean=-0.0022, sd=0.9855)\r\n    samples saved to /app/normal_samples.txt\r\n\r\n[2] Sampling 5000 draws from Exp(1) via ars(dexp, c(0, Inf)) ...\r\n    expected mean = 1, sd = 1; Kolmogorov-Smirnov p-value = 0.6230\r\nEXPONENTIAL_TEST: PASS (mean=0.9943, sd=0.9646)\r\n    samples saved to /app/exponential_samples.txt\r\n\r\n[3] Sampling 5000 draws from Gamma(shape=3) on (0, Inf) ...\r\n    expected mean = 3, sd = 1.7321; KS p-value = 0.7431\r\nGAMMA_TEST: PASS (mean=2.9893, sd=1.7137)\r\n\r\n[4] Sampling 3000 draws from an *unnormalized* normal kernel exp(-x^2/2) ...\r\nUNNORMALIZED_TEST: PASS (mean=0.0030, sd=1.0217)\r\n\r\n[5] Module test: upper hull dominates log-density, lower hull is dominated ...\r\nHULL_TEST: PASS (max(h-u)=0.00e+00, max(l-h)=0.00e+00)\r\n\r\n[6] Input validation: invalid inputs must raise errors ...\r\nINVALID_N_TEST: PASS (negative sample count rejected)\r\nINVALID_DOMAIN_TEST: PASS (reversed domain rejected)\r\nINVALID_DENSITY_TEST: PASS (non-function density rejected)\r\n\r\n[7] Non-log-concave densities must be detected during sampling ...\r\n    caught expected error: ars: non-log-concavity detected (log-density exceeds the upper hull)\r\nNON_LOG_CONCAVE_CAUCHY_TEST: PASS\r\n    caught expected error: ars: density is not log-concave (slope of log-density increased between abscissae)\r\nNON_LOG_CONCAVE_MIXTURE_TEST: PASS\r\n\r\n============================================================\r\n"]
[627.690869, "o", "OVERALL: ALL TESTS PASSED\r\n============================================================\r\n"]
